# A runnable tour of this API's response contract: every endpoint, failures included.
#
# JetBrains IDEs open this file natively. In VS Code, install the REST Client extension once:
#     code --install-extension humao.rest-client
# then click "Send Request" above any block. If you would rather use curl, the README has the
# equivalents — and reading this file straight through works too.
#
# Start the API first with `npm run dev`. Changed PORT? Update @host below to match.

@host = http://localhost:3002
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### Liveness — outside the version prefix
GET {{host}}/health

### List — defaults: page 1, 20 per page, sorted by title
GET {{api}}/book

### List — second page of five
GET {{api}}/book?page=2&pageSize=5

### List — newest first
GET {{api}}/book?sortBy=publishedYear&sortOrder=desc&pageSize=5

### List — search by title, case-insensitive
GET {{api}}/book?search=harbour

### List — 400: sortBy outside the whitelist
GET {{api}}/book?sortBy=acquisitionCost

### List — 400: pageSize above the cap of 100
GET {{api}}/book?pageSize=999

### Detail — 200, note the derived `available` and the absent acquisitionCost
GET {{api}}/book/book-001

### Detail — a book with no copies on the shelf: available is false
GET {{api}}/book/book-002

### Detail — 404 with the catalogue error code
GET {{api}}/book/does-not-exist

### Create — 201. Omitting copiesAvailable puts every copy on the shelf
POST {{api}}/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Ropemaker Variations",
  "authorName": "Ines Karadzic",
  "isbn": "9791234567890",
  "genre": "fiction",
  "publishedYear": 2024,
  "copiesTotal": 4
}

### Create — 409: that ISBN is already in the catalogue
POST {{api}}/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "A Second Copy",
  "authorName": "Ines Karadzic",
  "isbn": "9784100000000",
  "genre": "fiction",
  "publishedYear": 2024,
  "copiesTotal": 2
}

### Create — 400: more copies on the shelf than the library owns
POST {{api}}/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Impossible Inventory",
  "authorName": "Ines Karadzic",
  "isbn": "9791111111111",
  "genre": "essay",
  "publishedYear": 2020,
  "copiesTotal": 2,
  "copiesAvailable": 9
}

### Create — 400: per-field validation detail
POST {{api}}/book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "authorName": "X",
  "isbn": "123",
  "genre": "graphic-novel",
  "publishedYear": 1200,
  "copiesTotal": 0
}

### (not built yet) Record a loan — the endpoint you are asked to add
POST {{api}}/book/book-001/loan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "borrowerName": "Ada Whitfield"
}

### (not built yet) Record a loan on a book with no copies on the shelf — expect 409
POST {{api}}/book/book-002/loan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "borrowerName": "Ada Whitfield"
}

### 400, not 500, when the body is not valid JSON
# The body below is invalid on purpose: it never closes its brace. Sending broken JSON is the
# whole point of this request — a client that cannot be parsed must be told so, not handed a 500.
POST {{api}}/book
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "This body is missing its closing brace"

### 404 with the error envelope on an unknown route — last request in this file
GET {{api}}/nowhere
